# Enforce LF line endings for all text files, regardless of platform or
# editor settings. Without this, Windows checkouts can convert files to
# CRLF on clone/pull, which then fails `prettier --check` (Prettier
# defaults to LF) even though the actual committed content is correctly
# formatted -- every file in the repo can appear "wrong" at once, which is
# exactly this symptom, not a real formatting problem.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files that should never be line-ending-normalized.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ico binary
